  "id": "just-world-hypothesis",
  "term": "just-world hypothesis",
  "definition": "The just-world hypothesis is the belief that people generally get outcomes they deserve. In the research described here, stronger endorsement of this belief is associated with more victim-blaming, harsher moral judgments, and greater rationalization of inequality.",
